Known failure: range-stable — range formatting indents the interior lines of a multi-line string, comment, region body or code block inside a block, changing a string's value (feature.formatting A13; #325)
Multi-line tokens inside a procedure: a string, a comment, a :REGION body
and a code block keep their interior lines verbatim under full formatting
(fmt.indent_style, fmt.code_block_literals, feature.formatting A3).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Demo;
:DECLARE sText, fnDouble;
sText := "alpha
beta";
/* first line
second line;
:REGION Payload;
SELECT a FROM t
  WHERE b = 1
:ENDREGION;
fnDouble := {|nX| nX +
2};
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Demo;
	:DECLARE sText, fnDouble;
	sText := "alpha
beta";
	/* first line
second line;
	:REGION Payload;
SELECT a FROM t
  WHERE b = 1
	:ENDREGION;
	fnDouble := {|nX| nX +
2};
:ENDPROC;
